  "status_text": "Every five-gate design gets this six-light puzzle wrong somewhere. Number the lights from 1 to 6 and turn on exactly one or two. Say yes to light 1 alone, to 1 with 4, to 1 with 5, or to 2 with 3. Say no to every other allowed setting. Lean checked that no circuit of at most five AND, OR or NOT gates, each with at most two inputs, can give all 21 answers correctly. That rules out the five-gate proposal. Can six do it? (L-meta-25662, L-meta-22744)",
